-      <li><div><b>Train one fixed selector and test it elsewhere</b>A deterministic linear model reads 144 ray values plus proprioception and predicts whether each command will succeed. It is evaluated on twelve layouts it never saw, on all three carriers.</div></li>
+      <li><div><b>Execute the alternatives, don't imagine them</b>In an empty room the frozen SONIC tracker runs every command in a qualified repertoire — neutral walking plus six timed crouch schedules. We keep the achieved 50 Hz whole-body trajectories, not the references the controller was asked to track.</div></li>
+      <li><div><b>Place the obstacle where those executions disagree</b>A candidate scene is one where some schedule keeps clearance across all 81 placement offsets (the <em>positive</em> screen) and some other schedule nominally interferes (the <em>negative</em> screen). Geometry proposes; it never labels.</div></li>
