+    <p>Note the reverse case in row four: reference-envelope contrast runs 6/6, 5/6, 4/6 against screened uniform's flat 5/6, so it both beats and loses to the baseline depending on the seed. The only arm executed contrast beats is target-only, the weakest. Any "no reverse case" generalisation fails at this layer.</p>
+
+    <p>The strong scripted comparator passes 6 of 6 and sits at this panel's ceiling, so a tie in success count is a property of the panel, not evidence that the populations are equal. What the panel does establish is that the distinctive ingredient did not change behaviour: thirteen of fifteen learned policies collapsed to a constant schedule, and none passed anywhere the seven-schedule bank failed.</p>
+
+    <div class="headline">
+      <p>Reconciling the two generations gives the finding that actually survives. Executed-contrast construction beats <span class="em">unscreened</span> placement decisively, and does not beat <span class="em">feasibility-screened</span> placement at all. The part carrying the measured benefit is the <span class="em">positive executable-support screen</span>. The additional negative-interference targeting — the distinctive Motion2Scene ingredient — has no measured downstream effect.</p>
