-    <h3>One place the learned generator is measurably worse</h3>
-    <p>Its training loss is 0.139 against the analytic solver's 0.00054 on identical architecture and label count. The reason is in the construction record: only 24 of its 34 critical scenes are visible to the robot's sensor at the moment the command must be issued, against 44 of 47 for the analytic solver. A contrast the robot cannot see is a label the learner cannot fit. That is a specific, fixable defect, and no visibility filter was added after the fact to hide it.</p>
+    <p>Across 42 registered executions, reactive and scripted privileged crouching each pass 9 of 10 pose trials while all ten blind trials contact the beam. Blind walking still <em>crosses</em> under contact, so contact is not evidence of impassability — the criterion is contact-qualified passage, not mere arrival. The causal observation delay locates the timing budget directly: 100 ms and 260 ms both pass 2/2, while <strong>500 ms refuses and fails 2/2</strong>. Both reactive and oracle failures occur at the same condition — station −15 cm in the second seed, with a 429 N contact — so the limit is the geometry of that approach, not the sensing policy alone.</p>
