+        <p class="why">Branch-linked teacher and student data with hash-bound provenance is a genuine companion asset.</p>
+        <p>1,065 recorded captures across fifteen corpora, hash-bound registrations for every stage, and one portable release that is exported and offline-verifiable: 12 corpora, 276 episodes, 328,992 measured physics steps, reconstructed to a maximum coefficient difference of 5.55e-17. No M8, M16 or M32 release has been exported, and the archive-integrity counts are verification totals over that 276-episode slice, not dataset scale. What is missing is the part that makes a dataset paper: a demonstration that the corpus is useful to a <em>different</em> learner or robot, plus licensing and a public reproduction harness. The research compass is explicit that new-learner or new-robot utility requires additional evidence, and none has been collected.</p>
