-    <p class="sub">Five gates, in dependency order. Each has a measured starting point from this study.</p>
+    <h2>What remains</h2>
+    <p class="sub">In dependency order. Each item states what it would settle, not merely what it would produce.</p>
 
     <div class="road">
       <article>
-        <h3>1 · Re-price the contrast for a real obstacle pose</h3>
-        <p class="why">Because on hardware the beam's pose is uncertain, and this study deliberately assumed it is not.</p>
-        <p>The envelope sweep already states the cost: at ±20 mm only 2, 0 and 32 placements survive per carrier. A deployment needs either a much larger executed window, obtained by a deeper or slower adaptation, or obstacle localisation tight enough to make the nominal contract honest. Measure the achievable window against a real perception stack before building anything else.</p>
