-        <p>A deployed robot decides repeatedly as the scene resolves. Extending to sequential decisions changes the state distribution the selector sees, so it needs matched data aggregation across every arm and fresh labels, not a re-scored version of these. The timing result, where 0.20 s and 0.40 s both fail while 0.30 s passes, shows how narrow the admissible window already is.</p>
