+        <p class="why">Because the policy commits once from a fixed approach, and a real robot decides repeatedly.</p>
+        <p>Closing the loop changes the state distribution the learner sees, so it requires matched data aggregation across every arm and fresh labels. Only then does hardware become meaningful — and nothing here is a protective action: a refusal continues walking. The 1 N contact criterion is a simulation convention, not a safety margin. The C++ TensorRT runtime exists, but <strong>no Motion2Scene hardware transfer evidence exists at all</strong>.</p>
